The matrix indicies denote the $i$-th element in the bases, \emph{including} the odd-parity waves, i.e., only even values correspond to the $n$-th solution of the Busch formula in \equref{busch_formula}. The integral $\int_{-\infty}^\infty\d x\  f_{\nu_i}(x) \phi_j(x)$ can be explicitly calculated by exploiting the fact that $f_\nu$ is an eigenfunction of the Schr\"odinger equation, thus,
