Here $\gamma^\dagger_{n\sigma}$, $\gamma_{n\sigma}$ are creation and annihilation operators for quasiparticle excitations with spin $\sigma=\uparrow,\downarrow$. The Bogoliubov amplitudes are complex numbers; for convenience, we may define gauge by taking $u_{n} = u_{n}^*$, $v_{n} = |v_{n}|e^{i\varphi}$ with $\varphi$ being the phase of the order parameter, $\Delta=|\Delta|e^{i\varphi}$. To preserve canonical commutation relations, their magnitudes satisfy the constraint
\begin{equation}
