The variables $\hat{\xi}^a_{\pm}$ behave in many ways as creation and annihilation operators, but do not require a specific basis in phase space, which enables a compact covariant proof of Wick's theorem~\cite{hackl2020bosonic}. Moreover, $\hat{\xi}^a_{\pm}$ spans the $N$-dimensional complex eigenspaces $V^{\pm}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of $J$, which are the spaces of creation or annihilation operators associated to $\ket{J}$, respectively. We refer to $\hat{\xi}_\pm^a$ as phase space covariant creation and annihilation operators, which satisfy the following commutation (bosons) or anti-commutation (fermions) relations:
